    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NidJm7Tzd128tJp4sbpQtK)_\n\n`fish_greeting` in `.config/fish/config.fish` now runs `fastfetch` only when `INSIDE_EMACS` is unset. Shells started by Emacs (`shell`, `eat`, `M-x compile` with an interactive shell) set `INSIDE_EMACS`, so they no longer print or wait for the greeting.\n\nNote: `exec-path-from-shell` does not set `INSIDE_EMACS`, so its login shell still prints the greeting. Not confirmed as the cause of the start-up hang. Not run (no fish or Emacs in the container).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBTiUziZidcdSerB8r)_",
